REFERENCE — pvemanagerlib.js (pve-mac-monitor v2.5.0)
File: /usr/share/pve-manager/js/pvemanagerlib.js

A) Ext.define('PVE.node.StatusView')

  - status box height: any value < 400 is raised to 400 (350->400 on stock
    PVE 8/9). Larger values (e.g. 600 from proxmox-summary-enhancement) are
    left untouched, so both patches coexist.
  - rows inserted after the Manager Version row (textField: 'pveversion'),
    wrapped in // >>> pve-mac-monitor markers. Layout follows the
    pve-mac-monitor-orig.sh design: bar + spacer + peaks + spacer.

      1) bar row (valueField/maxField => native usage bar):
             {
                 iconCls: 'fa fa-fw fa-sitemap',
                 itemId: 'macstats',
                 title: gettext('Hetzner MAC Limit'),
                 valueField: 'mac_current',
                 maxField: 'mac_limit',
                 printBar: true,
                 warningThreshold: 0.84375,
                 criticalThreshold: 0.9375,
                 renderer: function(value, max) { ... "N / 32 (P%)" ... },
             },
         Proxmox.widget.Info compares strictly (usage > threshold), so a
         threshold sits one MAC below the level that must trigger it while
         staying above the previous level:
             criticalThreshold 0.9375  => 30/32 is below, 31/32 is critical (red)
             warningThreshold  0.84375 => 27/32 is below, 28/32 is warning (amber)
         criticalThreshold: 1.0 (as in the early prototype) never fires,
         because 32/32 > 1.0 is false.

      2) spacer cell:
             { xtype: 'box', html: '&nbsp;', padding: '0 10 5 10' },

      3) peaks row (textField passes the whole object to the renderer):
             {
                 iconCls: 'fa fa-fw fa-history',
                 itemId: 'macstats_peaks',
                 printBar: false,
                 title: gettext('MAC peaks'),
                 textField: 'macstats',
                 renderer: function(value) { ... 15m / 1h / 24h ... },
             },

      4) second spacer cell.

      textField is required for object-valued rows: InfoWidget.updateField
      only calls updateValue for multiField/textField/valueField rows. A
      renderer-only row stays empty without any error.

B) Ext.define('PVE.node.Summary')

  - model before the Summary define:
      // >>> pve-mac-monitor model BEGIN
      Ext.define('pve-rrd-mac', {
          extend: 'Ext.data.Model',
          fields: ['mac', { type: 'date', dateFormat: 'timestamp', name: 'time' }],
      });
      // <<< pve-mac-monitor model END

  - store before `var rrdstore = Ext.create('Proxmox.data.RRDStore', ...)`:
      // >>> pve-mac-monitor store BEGIN
      var macTimeframe = 'hour';           // defaults match RRDStore
      var macCf = 'average';               // both read from the
      // 'proxmoxRRDTypeSelection' state (same key the stock charts use)
      var macStore = Ext.create('Proxmox.data.UpdateStore', {
          interval: 60000,
          autoStart: true,
          model: 'pve-rrd-mac',
          storeid: 'pve-mac-history',
          proxy: { type: 'proxmox',
                   url: '/api2/json/nodes/' + nodename + '/mac-history'
                        + '?timeframe=' + macTimeframe + '&cf=' + macCf },
      });
      // statechange listener -> reload on Hour/Day/Week/Month/Year change
      // <<< pve-mac-monitor store END

  - chart appended to the Summary chart container's `items: [...]` array
    (after Memory Pressure Stall). On PVE 9 the charts live in a nested
    `xtype: 'container', itemId: 'itemcontainer'` column layout, so the
    patcher anchors on the last proxmoxRRDChart and picks the innermost
    enclosing items array instead of the outer panel items list:
      // >>> pve-mac-monitor chart BEGIN
      {
          title: gettext('MAC addresses (used)'),
          xtype: 'proxmoxRRDChart',
          fields: ['mac'],            // single series; cf picks average or max
          fieldTitles: [gettext('MACs')],
          store: macStore,
      },
      // <<< pve-mac-monitor chart END

  - panel lifecycle hooks (single lines marked `// pve-mac-monitor hook`):
      after rrdstore.startUpdate();  -> macStore.startUpdate();
      after rrdstore.stopUpdate();   -> macStore.stopUpdate();

Notes:
  - Same proxmoxRRDChart + UpdateStore + date-model pattern as the stock
    CPU/Memory charts, so bars, tooltips and the timeframe selector behave
    natively.
  - Insertion is whitespace-tolerant, appends to the end of the Summary items
    array, and is idempotent (blocks are rebuilt from markers on re-run).

Exact insertion logic: src/patch-mac-frontend.py
